":0.07703362281842453,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":3.7,"_gate_piotroski":8,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":88.9,"_gate_spread":-0.026797570036544753,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.892340497079117,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.07810503517937295,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.002141126408041011,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":32.6,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.014475197996405509,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":17.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.04554757878250141,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":4.5,"_gate_fund_growth":0.011343234811962604,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":11.3,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.011981313637013822,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":80.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.18683,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.214,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":21.4,"pf":[],"description_full":"LSB Industries, Inc. manufactures, markets, and sells chemical products in the United States. The company offers ammonia and urea ammonia nitrate for agricultural applications. It also provides high purity and commercial grade ammonia, high purity ammonium nitrate, sulfuric acids, concentrated, blended and regular nitric acid, mixed nitrating acids, carbon dioxide, industrial grade ammonium nitrate, and ammonium nitrate for industrial applications. It sells its products to farmers, ranchers, fertilizer dealers, and distributors primarily in the ranch land and grain production markets, as well as industrial users of acids and explosive manufacturers. LSB Industries, Inc. was founded in 1968 and is headquartered in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark T. Behrman | President, CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 62 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 513 people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $35K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $14K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["LSB Industries, Inc. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $763M market cap on $615M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -12% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 15% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $18M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.88\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (79% sell ratio, net $76.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 66/100): roic below cost of capital; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Basic Materials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Basic Materials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 27% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Financial quality scores above most Basic Materials peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in LXU Response","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/24/Discipline_and_Rules-Based_Execution_in_LXU_Response_110226101401_1793632441.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793632441.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Ecolab (NYSE:ECL) versus Lsb Industries (NYSE:LXU) Head to Head Analysis","s